+## Context
+
+New TypeScript library with no runtime dependencies; tests run with `node --test`. Later features will reuse the pointer parsing.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** a strict RFC 6901 `resolvePointer`; parsing separated from resolution so later features can reuse it.
+**Non-Goals:** the URI fragment representation (`#/...`), relative pointers, and writing values.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Internal `parsePointer(pointer): string[]` validates and unescapes tokens; `resolvePointer` walks them. Both live in `src/index.ts` (only `resolvePointer` is exported), because Node type stripping cannot resolve `.js` imports to `.ts` files.
+- Own-property check (`Object.hasOwn`) for objects, so `__proto__`/`constructor` never resolve.
+- Array index must match `/^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$/` and be less than the length; `-` always throws, since it refers to a nonexistent element.
+- Missing and invalid cases throw `Error` (a plain message naming the pointer/token).
+- Tests live in `src/index.test.ts`, run by `node --test` through Node type stripping, and are excluded from `tsconfig.json`.
